IMPORT prelude

-- Intestate Succession Act 1967 (Singapore) -- who inherits when a person dies without a will (or with a will that does not dispose
-- of everything): to whom the Act applies (s 2), who counts as a "child" (s 3), which law governs (ss 4, 5), the treatment of
-- maternal, paternal, posthumous and half-blood relatives (s 6), the nine rules of distribution (s 7), more than one widow (s 8),
-- lifetime gifts to children (s 9), and partial intestacy (s 10). That is the whole operative Act.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ISA1967.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later amendment is annotated in
-- the text. The accompanying metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it decides who inherits the estate of every non-Muslim who dies in Singapore
-- without a will. Not by citation count. Not encoded: the Probate and Administration Act 1934 (who administers, the "expenses of due
-- administration" deducted under s 5), the Muslim law excluded by s 2, the law of any foreign domicile under s 4(1), and the
-- Legitimacy Act or Adoption of Children Act (not read). Shares are modelled as dollar amounts of the net estate; the Act's own
-- reversionary-interest language in rule 3 is not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Intestate Succession Act 1967 -- distribution`

§§ `2, 4, 5 -- whose property passes under this Act`

-- s 2: "Nothing in this Act shall apply to the estate of any Muslim".
-- s 4(1): movable property -- "regulated by the law of the country in which he was domiciled at the time of his death".
-- s 4(2): immovable property -- "regulated by this Act wherever he may have been domiciled".
-- s 5: a person who "dies intestate after 2 June 1967" being (a) "domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property,
-- whether movable or immovable ... situated in Singapore"; or (b) "domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of
-- immovable property situated in Singapore" -- that property, "after payment thereout of the expenses of due administration as
-- prescribed by the Probate and Administration Act 1934", is distributed under the Act.
-- The date of death is written as a number YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `the deceased was a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `date of death` IS A NUMBER,
      `domiciled in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the property is immovable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the property is situated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is distributed under this Act` IF
        (NOT `the deceased was a Muslim`)
    AND `date of death` GREATER THAN 19670602
    AND `the property is situated in Singapore`
    AND (`domiciled in Singapore` OR `the property is immovable`)

§§ `3, 6(a) -- who counts as a child`

-- s 3: "'child' means a legitimate child and includes any child adopted by virtue of an order of court under any written law for
-- the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam"; "'issue' includes children and the descendants of deceased
-- children".
-- s 6(a): no distinction between relatives through the father and through the mother, "nor between those who were actually born in
-- his lifetime and those who at the date of his death were only conceived in the womb but who have subsequently been born alive".
DECLARE AdoptionPlace IS ONE OF
    `not adopted`
    `adopted by court order in Singapore`
    `adopted by court order in Malaysia`
    `adopted by court order in Brunei`
    `adopted elsewhere`

GIVEN `legitimate` IS A BOOLEAN, `adoption` IS AN AdoptionPlace
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as a child of the deceased` IF
        `legitimate`
    OR  CONSIDER `adoption`
        WHEN `adopted by court order in Singapore` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `adopted by court order in Malaysia` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `adopted by court order in Brunei` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6, 7, 8 -- the family that survives`

-- The surviving family, counted for the rules of distribution.
--   `child stocks`: the children who survive plus the children who died before the intestate leaving descendants (rule 3, provisos
--   (1) and (2): descendants "stand in the place of their parent" and "take according to their stocks").
--   `sibling stocks`: whole-blood brothers and sisters who survive plus deceased whole-blood brothers and sisters who left children
--   (rule 6).
--   `half-blood sibling stocks`: the same, of the half blood. s 6(b): "those related to a person deceased by the half blood shall rank
--   immediately after those of the whole blood related to him in the same degree". INFERENCE: half-blood siblings take under rule 6
--   only if there is no whole-blood sibling stock, and they still exclude grandparents. The Act does not say this in terms.
--   `spouses surviving`: s 8 lets more than one widow share.
DECLARE Family HAS
    `spouses surviving` IS A NUMBER
    `child stocks` IS A NUMBER
    `parents surviving` IS A NUMBER
    `sibling stocks` IS A NUMBER
    `half-blood sibling stocks` IS A NUMBER
    `grandparents surviving` IS A NUMBER
    `uncles and aunts surviving` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a spouse, issue or parent` IF
        `fam`'s `spouses surviving` GREATER THAN 0
    OR  `fam`'s `child stocks` GREATER THAN 0
    OR  `fam`'s `parents surviving` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a sibling stock of either blood` IF
        `fam`'s `sibling stocks` GREATER THAN 0
    OR  `fam`'s `half-blood sibling stocks` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `7 rules 1, 2, 4 and 8 -- the surviving spouse`

-- Rule 1: "surviving spouse, no issue and no parent, the spouse shall be entitled to the whole of the estate".
-- Rule 2: "surviving spouse and issue, the spouse shall be entitled to one-half of the estate".
-- Rule 4: "surviving spouse and no issue but a parent or parents, the spouse shall be entitled to one-half ... and the parent or
-- parents to the other half".
-- Nothing about brothers and sisters: a spouse with no issue and no parent takes everything, whoever else survives.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouses' combined share` MEANS
    IF `fam`'s `spouses surviving` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `fam`'s `child stocks` GREATER THAN 0 OR `fam`'s `parents surviving` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `estate` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE `estate`

-- s 8: "If any person so dying intestate leaves surviving him more than one wife, such wives shall share among them equally the share
-- that the wife of the intestate would have been entitled to, had the intestate left only one wife surviving him."
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each spouse's share` MEANS
    IF `fam`'s `spouses surviving` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `the spouses' combined share` `estate` `fam` DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `spouses surviving`

§§ `7 rule 3 -- issue, per stirpes`

-- Rule 3: "Subject to the rights of the surviving spouse, if any, the estate ... of an intestate who leaves issue shall be distributed
-- by equal portions per stirpes to and amongst the children ... and such persons as legally represent those children, in case any of
-- those children be then dead." Proviso (1): those who legally represent the children "are their descendants and not their
-- next-of-kin". Proviso (2): descendants "take according to their stocks the share which he or she would have taken".
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each child stock's share` MEANS
    IF `fam`'s `child stocks` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE (`estate` MINUS `the spouses' combined share` `estate` `fam`) DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `child stocks`

-- A grandchild whose parent (the intestate's child) died first shares that parent's stock equally with its brothers and sisters.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family, `grandchildren in the stock` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each grandchild's share in a deceased child's stock` MEANS
    `each child stock's share` `estate` `fam` DIVIDED BY `grandchildren in the stock`

§§ `7 rules 4 and 5 -- parents`

-- Rule 5: "If there are no descendants, the parent or parents of the intestate shall take the estate, in equal portions if there be 2
-- parents, subject to the rights of the surviving spouse (if any) as provided in rule 4." Where there is issue, rule 2 and rule 3
-- dispose of the whole estate, and the parents take nothing.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each parent's share` MEANS
    IF `fam`'s `child stocks` GREATER THAN 0 OR `fam`'s `parents surviving` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE (`estate` MINUS `the spouses' combined share` `estate` `fam`) DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `parents surviving`

§§ `6(b), 7 rule 6 -- brothers and sisters, and their children`

-- Rule 6: "If there are no surviving spouse, descendants or parents, the brothers and sisters and children of deceased brothers or
-- sisters of the intestate shall share the estate in equal portions ... and the children of any deceased brother or sister shall take
-- according to their stocks the share which the deceased brother or sister would have taken."
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each whole-blood sibling stock's share` MEANS
    IF `there is a spouse, issue or parent` `fam` OR `fam`'s `sibling stocks` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `estate` DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `sibling stocks`

-- s 6(b), read as an INFERENCE: the half blood take only when no whole-blood sibling stock exists.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each half-blood sibling stock's share` MEANS
    IF `there is a spouse, issue or parent` `fam` OR `fam`'s `sibling stocks` GREATER THAN 0 OR `fam`'s `half-blood sibling stocks` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `estate` DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `half-blood sibling stocks`

-- A nephew or niece whose parent (the intestate's whole-blood brother or sister) died first.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family, `nephews and nieces in the stock` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each nephew's or niece's share in a deceased sibling's stock` MEANS
    `each whole-blood sibling stock's share` `estate` `fam` DIVIDED BY `nephews and nieces in the stock`

§§ `7 rules 7, 8 and 9 -- grandparents, uncles and aunts, and the Government`

-- Rule 7: no spouse, descendants, parents, brothers and sisters or their children "but grandparents ... the grandparents shall take
-- the whole of the estate in equal portions".
-- Rule 8: none of those and no grandparents "but uncles and aunts ... the uncles and aunts shall take the whole of the estate in equal
-- portions".
-- Rule 9: "In default of distribution under rules 1 to 8, the Government shall be entitled to the whole of the estate."
-- No rule reaches cousins, great-nephews, great-uncles or step-relatives.
GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each grandparent's share` MEANS
    IF `there is a spouse, issue or parent` `fam` OR `there is a sibling stock of either blood` `fam` OR `fam`'s `grandparents surviving` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `estate` DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `grandparents surviving`

GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each uncle's or aunt's share` MEANS
    IF     `there is a spouse, issue or parent` `fam` OR `there is a sibling stock of either blood` `fam`
        OR `fam`'s `grandparents surviving` GREATER THAN 0 OR `fam`'s `uncles and aunts surviving` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `estate` DIVIDED BY `fam`'s `uncles and aunts surviving`

GIVEN `estate` IS A NUMBER, `fam` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share` MEANS
    IF     `there is a spouse, issue or parent` `fam` OR `there is a sibling stock of either blood` `fam`
        OR `fam`'s `grandparents surviving` GREATER THAN 0 OR `fam`'s `uncles and aunts surviving` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `estate`

§§ `9 -- lifetime gifts to children are not deducted`

-- s 9: where a child or a child's descendant claims a distributive share, "no money or other property which the intestate may during
-- his life have given, paid or settled to or for the advancement of the child ... shall be taken into account in estimating such
-- distributive share".
GIVEN `share under the rules` IS A NUMBER, `lifetime gifts for advancement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the child's distributive share after lifetime gifts` MEANS
    `share under the rules`

§§ `10 -- partial intestacy`

-- s 3: "'intestate' includes any person who leaves a will but dies intestate as to some beneficial interest in his property".
-- s 10: the Act "shall have effect as respects the part of his property not so disposed of, subject to the provisions contained in
-- the will"; proviso: the personal representative is "a trustee for the persons entitled under this Act in respect of the part of the
-- estate not expressly disposed of unless it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part
-- beneficially".
GIVEN `the will disposes of this part` IS A BOOLEAN, `the will shows the personal representative takes it beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this part passes under the Act` IF
        (NOT `the will disposes of this part`)
    AND (NOT `the will shows the personal representative takes it beneficially`)
